# Git Conventions

## Repository

- GitHub: `thisissuman/wed-pro` — `https://github.com/thisissuman/wed-pro.git`

## Branching (GitHub Flow)

| Branch | Use |
|--------|-----|
| `main` | Production-ready; deployable to Vercel |
| `feat/*` | New features |
| `fix/*` | Bug fixes |
| `chore/*` / `refactor/*` | Tooling, deps, refactors |

**Never push directly to `main`.** Use PR or fast-forward merge when solo.

## Commits (Conventional Commits)

```
<type>(<optional scope>): <description>
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `chore`

- Imperative mood: "Add editor" not "Added editor"
- Atomic commits — don't mix unrelated changes

Examples:
- `feat(templates): add royal template sections`
- `fix(preview): resolve countdown hydration mismatch`
- `chore(config): update next.config.ts`

## `.gitignore` (must never commit)

`node_modules/`, `.next/`, `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.*.local`, `.DS_Store`, `coverage/`

## Supabase Schema

- Avoid structural prod changes only in Supabase UI
- Use Supabase CLI locally; commit SQL in `supabase/migrations/`
- Example: `supabase migration new add_invitations_table`

## Merge

Rebase/merge `main` before merge; prefer **Squash and Merge**; self-review diffs for `console.log` and commented code.

## Assets

Compress images in `/public` (WebP/AVIF); no 10MB raw photos in git.
